# Ledger

Before creating or retaining L, apply the [common content decision](../../framework/rules/records.md#substantive-material-retention).
An adequate existing home needs no duplicate; L records substantive exploration, comparison, synthesis and eligible findings, rather than allocation or move history.
Follow the [kind-specific rules](../../framework/rules/ledger.md#substantive-mathematical-operations).

L retains exploration, useful failures, comparisons, syntheses and suitable self-review or unknown-relationship findings.
A Claim's argument belongs to fixed C; independent project-review accounts belong to fixed R, including partial or unadopted findings.
Follow the [material-role rules](../../framework/rules/claims.md#record-kinds) and [review rules](../../framework/rules/proof-audits.md).

See the [current index](index.md) and [framework rules](../../framework/readme.md).
